  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid response to mitigate the negative impact of protracted drought on health in Banadir, Bay, Lower Shabelle and Middle Shabelle regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $3m WHO projects aims to provide life-saving health and nutrition interventions to drought-affected Somalis. To that end, WHO will provide essential primary healthcare, including vaccination, malnutrition screening and antenatal care services, equip health facilities with supplies and medicines and ensure quality service, and strengthen disease surveillance. In total, WHO will target 92,308 people, including 17,078 women and 28,615 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
